      <title>Hildon App. Manager: package management for Internet Tablets</title>
      <subtitle></subtitle>
      <track>Lightning Talks</track>
      <type></type>
      <language></language>
      <abstract>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Debian-style package management for maemo consumers&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;    - For applications, for the operating system.&#xA;    - For hackers, for grandmas (and hacking grandmas).&#xA;    - Challenge: easy and robust configuration management on the device.&#xA;    - Challenge: traditional monolithic development and release process&#xA;      for mobile devices: OS as binary blob, no dependencies between&#xA;      applications.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Our approaches to the challenges will be explained briefly.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA; </abstract>
      <description>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The Hildon Application Manager is pre-installed on all&#xA;           Internet Tablets and handles the installation and removal&#xA;           of additional software.  In the future, it will also keep&#xA;           the operating system itself up-to-date.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;           The Application Manager is a frontend to apt and dpkg, like&#xA;           Synaptic or gnome-app-install, only different.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA; </description>
      <persons>
          <person id="401">Marius Vollmer</person>
